    "title": "This online database aims to revive Indigenous language before its last speakers are gone - NewsBreak",
    "text": "8 hours ago I was hired at the University of Colorado Boulder in 1995 as a language professor. I relocated from Hawaii, where I had learned the Hawaiian language. When I arrived in Colorado, I decided I needed to learn about the Indigenous language of the Boulder and Denver area, Arapaho. The Arapaho people had occupied the area for many years until they were forced to leave in the 1860s. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 5",
